research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md:206:Higher derivatives are the recursive objects of [[def-higher-derivatives-and-smoothness]]. Darboux's theorem ([[thm-darboux-theorem-for-derivatives]]) concerns every first derivative, without assuming that derivative continuous. The two L'Hôpital theorems, [[thm-lhopital-zero-over-zero]] and [[thm-lhopital-infinity-over-infinity]], require their stated derivative and nonvanishing hypotheses and do not assert converses.
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-207-
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md:208:Endpoint derivatives and finite-endpoint limits are one-sided when the domain supplies only one side. Natural factorials and binomial coefficients ([[def-factorial-and-falling-factorial]], [[def-binomial-coefficient]]) enter real formulas through the canonical embedding $\iota$ of [[def-canonical-natural]]. Darboux's property alone has no general continuity converse; the page's [[cor-injective-or-monotone-derivative-is-continuous]] proves continuity under the stated injectivity or monotonicity hypotheses.
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-209-
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-210-The Schlömilch-Roche formula ([[thm-taylor-schlomilch-roche-remainder]]) assumes
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-211-an $(n+1)$-st derivative on an interval. Peano's formula
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-212-([[thm-taylor-peano-remainder]]) assumes $n$-fold differentiability on an
research/audit/wave11-certifier-tasks/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md-213-open interval $N_\delta(a)$ around the expansion point
